| 0.5 | −9.641 | −9.876 | 27.834 |
| 1.0 | −9.921 | −7.586 | 29.015 |
| 2.0 | −4.398 | 1.522 | 26.547 |
| 3.0 | 6.311 | 8.744 | 23.476 |
| 5.0 | 11.244 | 7.433 | 30.712 |

By the symmetry $(x,y,z)\mapsto(-x,-y,z)$ of the system, this is the mirror image of trajectory ②, confirming the symmetric structure.

---

### 4. Description of the plots

Plotting any of the three trajectories in the $(x,z)$-plane (or 3-D $(x,y,z)$) over $t\in[0,50]$ yields the **Lorenz attractor**: two lobes centered near $E_{+}$ and $E_{-}$, connected at the origin.

- **Near $E_{0}$**: the trajectory leaves the origin along the unstable manifold (eigenvector of $\lambda_{1}\approx 11.827$), spirals around one lobe, then chaotically alternates between lobes with no periodic repetition.
- **Near $E_{+}$ / $E_{-}$**: each orbit initially spirals outward around its respective equilibrium (the unstable complex-conjugate pair of the saddle-focus), then is ejected and merges into the same strange attractor.

All three initial conditions converge to the same bounded, fractal, non-periodic attracting set — the Lorenz strange attractor — confirming that for $a=10,\,b=8/3,\,r=28$ no stable equilibrium exists and the long-term dynamics are chaotic.

---

### Summary

| Equilibrium | Coordinates | Eigenvalues (approx.) | Stability |
|---|---|---|---|
| $E_{0}$ | $(0,0,0)$ | $11.827,\;-22.827,\;-2.667$ | saddle (unstable) |
| $E_{+}$ | $(6\sqrt2,6\sqrt2,27)$ | $0.094\pm10.19i,\;-13.85$ | saddle-focus (unstable) |
| $E_{-}$ | $(-6\sqrt2,-6\sqrt2,27)$ | $0.094\pm10.19i,\;-13.85$ | saddle-focus (unstable) |

(The complex pair for $E_{\pm}$ has positive real part $\approx+0.094$ since $r=28>r_{H}\approx24.74$.) Numerical RK4 integration from points near each equilibrium all relax onto the Lorenz strange attractor.

